        "original_id": "21c17176-970a-5dab-87b8-b13ec1844409",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shreveport, Louisiana; Red River; Tybee Island, Georgia; Atlantic Ocean\n- Structures: Long–Allen Bridge\n- Roads: U.S. Route 80; Dixie Overland Highway\n- People: Huey Long; Oscar K. Allen\n\nFacts:\n- In 1933, the Long–Allen Bridge opened in Shreveport, Louisiana.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge is a truss bridge in Shreveport, Louisiana.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge was named for Louisiana governors Huey Long and Oscar K. Allen.\n- The Long–Allen Bridge carries U.S. Route 80 across the Red River.\n- U.S. Route 80 is an east–west United States Numbered Highway.\n- Much of U.S. Route 80 was once part of the early auto trail called the Dixie Overland Highway.\n- The eastern terminus of U.S. Route 80 is in Tybee Island, Georgia, at the intersection of Butler Avenue, Inlet Avenue, and Tybrisa Street near the Atlantic Ocean.",
